  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., falling from ~76 to ~68) followed by low or neutral sentiment, the model systematically underestimates the immediate rebound magnitude and direction.",
    "The model exhibits severe lag in detecting sudden volatility spikes; when true outcomes jump +30-40 points within 5 days, the forecast remains flat or slowly rising for weeks.",
    "After a sharp upward spike in price (e.g., >80), the model fails to predict the subsequent mean reversion and instead forecasts continued gradual growth.",
    "In high-volatility regimes with mixed sentiment, the model's 30-day horizon is biased toward a smoothed average that ignores short-term momentum reversals.",
    "When sentiment history contains isolated positive spikes (e.g., 1.00) amidst otherwise neutral data, the model should apply a temporary upward bias correction to avoid underestimating immediate rallies."
  ]
}
